<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Yihong Luo     Tianyang Hu     Jing Tang
</span><span id="id1" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_correspondence ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span>Corresponding Author.</span></span></span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span> CUHK (SZ)
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span> HKUST (GZ)
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">HKUST
</span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">While reinforcement learning methods such as Group Relative Preference Optimization (GRPO) have significantly enhanced Large Language Models, adapting them to diffusion models remains challenging.
In particular, GRPO demands a stochastic policy, yet the most cost‑effective diffusion samplers are based on deterministic ODEs.
Recent work addresses this issue by using inefficient SDE-based samplers to induce stochasticity, but this reliance on model-agnostic Gaussian noise leads to slow convergence.
To resolve this conflict, we propose Direct Group Preference Optimization (DGPO), a new online RL algorithm that dispenses with the policy-gradient framework entirely.
DGPO learns directly from group-level preferences, which utilize relative information of samples within groups.
This design eliminates the need for inefficient stochastic policies, unlocking the use of efficient deterministic ODE samplers and faster training.
Extensive results show that DGPO trains around 20 times faster than existing state-of-the-art methods and achieves superior performance on both in-domain and out-of-domain reward metrics.
Code is available at <a href="https://github.com/Luo-Yihong/DGPO" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/Luo-Yihong/DGPO</a>.</p>
  
</div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="p1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:24.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S0.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S0.F1.2" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:230.5pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08425v1/teaser_left_large_font.svg" id="S0.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:318/182;" width="318" height="182"></object>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="S0.F1.3" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:151.0pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08425v1/teaser_right_compact_large_font.svg" id="S0.F1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:209/179;" width="209" height="179"></object>
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Our proposed <span id="S0.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DGPO</span> shows a near 30 times faster training compared to Flow-GRPO on improving GenEval score (Left Figure). The notable improvement is achieved while maintaining strong performance on other out-of-domain metrics (Right Figure). </figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reinforcement Learning (RL) has become a cornerstone for the post-training of Large Language Models (LLMs), significantly enhancing their capabilities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ziegler et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. In particular, methods like Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> have demonstrated remarkable success in substantially improving the complex reasoning abilities of LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2025</a>)</cite>. However, progress in applying RL for post-training diffusion models has lagged considerably behind that of language models, leaving a significant gap in methods for aligning generative models with human preferences and complex quality metrics.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A central obstacle is the mismatch between GRPO’s policy gradient-based framework (short for policy framework in the following) and the mechanics of diffusion generation.
GRPO requires access to a stochastic policy to enable effective training and exploration.
This requirement is naturally met by LLMs, which inherently output a probability distribution over a vocabulary.
In contrast, diffusion models predominantly rely on deterministic ODE-based samplers to strike a better balance between sample quality and cost <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al., 2025c</a>)</cite>, and thus do not naturally provide a stochastic policy.
To bridge this gap, prior work has resorted to a forced adaptation: using stochastic SDE-based sampling to induce a conditional Gaussian policy suitable for GRPO’s policy framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xue et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
This workaround, however, introduces severe negative consequences:
(1) SDE-based rollouts are less efficient than their ODE counterparts and produce lower-quality samples under a fixed computational budget <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2022a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2022b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bao et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2020</a>)</cite>;
(2) The policy’s stochasticity comes from model-agnostic Gaussian noise, which provides a weak learning signal and results in slow convergence;
and (3) Training is performed over the entire sampling trajectory, making each iteration computationally expensive and time-consuming.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We argue that the practical success of GRPO stems less from its policy-gradient formulation, and more from its ability to utilize fine-grained relative preference information within group. Based on the insight, an ideal RL method for diffusion models should be capable of leveraging this powerful group-level information while dispensing with the need for a stochastic policy and its associated negative effects.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.08425v1/main_compare_new.png" id="S1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/351;" width="548" height="351" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Qualitative comparisons of DGPO against competing methods. It can be seen that our proposed DGPO not only accurately follows the instructions, but also keeps a strong visual quality.
All images are generated by the same initial noise.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To this end, we introduce <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">D</span>irect <span id="S1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">G</span>roup <span id="S1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P</span>reference <span id="S1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">O</span>ptimization (<span id="S1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DGPO</span>), a new online RL method tailored to diffusion models.
DGPO circumvents the policy-gradient framework entirely, instead optimizing the model by directly learning from the group-level preference between a set of “good” samples and a set of “bad” samples.
Concretely, for each prompt, we generate <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> samples using efficient ODE-based rollouts, partition them into positive and negative groups, and directly optimize the model by maximizing the likelihood of these group-wise preferences. Conceptually, DGPO can be understood as a natural extension of Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wallace et al., 2024</a>)</cite> that incorporates group-wise information, and as a diffusion-native re-imagination of GRPO.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This proposed methodology allows us to bypass the dependency on a stochastic policy, which yields several benefits:
(1) <span id="S1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficient Sampling and Learning</span>: by using high-fidelity ODE samplers, DGPO learns from higher-quality rollouts, leading to more effective learning.
(2) <span id="S1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficient Convergence</span>:
optimization is directly guided by group-level preferences rather than inefficient model-agnostic random exploration, leading to faster convergence.
(3) <span id="S1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficient Training</span>:
our approach avoids training on the entire sampling trajectory, notably reducing the computational cost of each training iteration. Together, these advantages establish DGPO as a highly efficient and powerful online RL algorithm for diffusion models.
Our extensive experiments show that DGPO achieves around 20× faster training than prior state-of-the-art Flow-GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, while delivering superior performance on both in-domain and out-of-domain metrics.
Most notably, on the challenging GenEval benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ghosh et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, DGPO trains nearly 30× faster than Flow-GRPO and boosts the base model’s performance from 63% to 97% (<a href="#S0.F1" title="In Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
These compelling results demonstrate DGPO’s potential as a powerful technique for aligning diffusion models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diffusion Models (DMs)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite> define a forward diffusion mechanism that progressively introduces Gaussian noise to input data <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> across <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> sequential timesteps. The forward process follows the distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})\triangleq\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{x}}_{t};\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}},\sigma_{t}^{2}\textbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{x}}_{t}|{\mathbf{x}})\triangleq\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{x}}_{t};\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}},\sigma_{t}^{2}\textbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, where the hyperparameters <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> control the noise scheduling strategy.
At each timestep, noisy samples are obtained by <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}+\sigma_{t}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}+\sigma_{t}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The parameterized reversed diffusion process is defined by:
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t})\triangleq\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1};\mu_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\textbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">I</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t})\triangleq\mathcal{N}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1};\mu_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\textbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The model’s neural network <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is learned by denoising <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},\epsilon,t}\lambda_{t}||f_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t)-{\mathbf{x}}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{x}},\epsilon,t}\lambda_{t}||f_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t)-{\mathbf{x}}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that the flow matching and DMs are equivalent in the context of diffusing by Gaussian noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward Modeling</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given ranked pairs generated from certain conditioning <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}\succ{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}\succ{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the “better” and “worse” samples. The Bradley-Terry (BT) model formulates the preferences as:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{BT}}({\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}\succ{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})=\sigma(r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0})-r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>BT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>≻</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{BT}}({\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}\succ{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})=\sigma(r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0})-r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sigmoid function. A network <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> that models reward can be trained by maximum likelihood as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{BT}}(\phi)=-\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}}\left[\log\sigma\left(r_{\phi}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0})-r_{\phi}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0})\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>BT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{BT}}(\phi)=-\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}}\left[\log\sigma\left(r_{\phi}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0})-r_{\phi}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RLHF</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RLHF typically aims to
optimize a conditional density <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math> to maximize a underlying reward <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> while staying close to a reference distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> via KL regularization, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{p_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\sim p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}\left[r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})\right]-\beta\mathrm{KL}\left[p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\|p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{p_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\sim p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}\left[r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})\right]-\beta\mathrm{KL}\left[p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\|p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the hyperparameter <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> controls strength of regularization.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GRPO Objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite></h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The RLHF objective in <a href="#S2.E3" title="In RLHF ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> can be optimized by policy-based learning (we omit the KL term and clip term hereinafter for brevity):</p>
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\max_{p_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{({\mathbf{x}}_{0},{\mathbf{x}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbf{x}}_{T})\sim p_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{c}})}\sum_{k=0}^{T}\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{k},{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\theta_{\text{old}}}({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{k},{\mathbf{c}})}A({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></munder><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{p_{\theta}}\mathbb{E}_{({\mathbf{x}}_{0},{\mathbf{x}}_{1},\cdots,{\mathbf{x}}_{T})\sim p_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{c}})}\sum_{k=0}^{T}\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{k},{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\theta_{\text{old}}}({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{k},{\mathbf{c}})}A({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the advantage of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be directly computed by reward <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r({\mathbf{x}}_{k+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, or introduce additional value model for reducing variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The GRPO proposes to sample a group of outputs for each prompt <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the old policy, then compute the advantage of each sample by normalization among groups, i.e., <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=(r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{r_{1},r_{2},\cdots,r_{G}\}))/{\text{std}(\{r_{1},r_{2},\cdots,r_{G}\})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mtext>std</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=(r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{r_{1},r_{2},\cdots,r_{G}\}))/{\text{std}(\{r_{1},r_{2},\cdots,r_{G}\})}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The policy learning requires that the transition between <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{k+1}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a stochastic distribution.
To meet this requirement for a stochastic policy, recent works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xue et al., 2025</a>)</cite> employ a stochastic SDE for sampling, rather than the more efficient deterministic ODE.
However, the SDE itself is less effective in sampling high-quality samples with insufficient steps.
Besides, the policy-based method requires performing training on the whole trajectory, which further leads to slow training.
More importantly, unlike LLMs, which directly output distribution, <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the stochasticity in DM’s policy comes from model-agnostic Gaussian Noise. This makes the stochastic exploration rely on the model-agnostic Gaussian noise, which is extremely inefficient in high-dimensional space. </span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DPO Objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2024</a>)</cite></h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unique global optimal density <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> of the RLHF objective (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In RLHF ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is given by:</p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})=p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\exp\left(r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})/\beta\right)/Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})=p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\exp\left(r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})/\beta\right)/Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}}p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\exp\left(r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})/\beta\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}}p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})\exp\left(r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})/\beta\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is a intractable partition function. We can compute the reward function as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})=\beta\log\frac{p^{*}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\beta\log Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})=\beta\log\frac{p^{*}_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\beta\log Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">After obtaining the parameterization of the reward function, the DPO optimizes the models by the reward learning objective in <a href="#S2.E2" title="In Reward Modeling ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>:</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{DPO}}(\theta)\!=\!-\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}-\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{DPO}}(\theta)\!=\!-\mathbb{E}_{{\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0},{\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}}\left[\log\sigma\left(\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}^{w}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}-\beta\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}^{l}_{0}|{\mathbf{c}})}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Diffusion DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wallace et al., 2024</a>)</cite> has adapted DPO to Diffusion models by defining reward over the diffusion paths <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}</annotation></semantics></math>, which does not require a stochastic policy.
<span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">However, it strictly relies on pairwise samples for optimization due to the intrinsic restriction of the intractable partition <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>, preventing the use of the fine-grained preference information of each sample.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Method</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We believe that the key to GRPO’s success lies in its ability to utilize fine-grained relative preference information within groups.
However, existing GRPO-style methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xue et al., 2025</a>)</cite> require using an inefficient stochastic policy.
Although existing DPO-style methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wallace et al., 2024</a>)</cite> provide a framework without the need for a stochastic policy, they require performing training on pairwise samples to eliminate the intractable partition <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
To this end, we propose Direct Group Preference Optimization (DGPO), which eliminates the inefficient stochastic policy and allows us to directly optimize inter-group preferences without concerning ourselves with an intractable partition, leveraging fine-grained reward information to significantly improve training efficiency. The pseudo code of DGPO is summarized in <a href="#alg1" title="In 3.1 Direct Group Preference Optimization ‣ 3 Method ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Problem Setup</h4>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote a pre-trained reference diffusion model with parameter <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have a dataset of conditions <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{c}=\{{\mathbf{c}}_{i=1}^{N}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐜</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{c}=\{{\mathbf{c}}_{i=1}^{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and a reward function <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\phi}(\cdot,\cdot):\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\phi}(\cdot,\cdot):\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{C}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that evaluates the quality of generated samples <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> given condition <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{c}}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{c}}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Our goal is to enhance a diffusion model <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, initialized from <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, according to the reward signal. At each training iteration, we use an online model <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta^{-}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{-}}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate a group of samples conditioned on <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{D}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{D}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> can be set as the current parameters <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> or an exponential moving average (EMA) version of previous <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>’s. These generated samples form a dataset
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(\mathcal{G}_{i}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{k=1}^{G}\},{\mathbf{c}}_{i})\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{k}\sim p_{\theta^{-}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{c}}_{i})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐜</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(\mathcal{G}_{i}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{k=1}^{G}\},{\mathbf{c}}_{i})\mid{\mathbf{x}}_{k}\sim p_{\theta^{-}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{c}}_{i})\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
which are then evaluated by the reward function to provide reward signals for splitting positive or negative groups.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Direct Group Preference Optimization</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In order to leverage relative information within groups, we propose directly learn the group-level preferences using the Bradley-Terry model via maximum likelihood:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log p(\mathcal{G}^{+}\succ\mathcal{G}^{-}|{\mathbf{c}})=\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(R_{\theta}(\mathcal{G}^{+}|{\mathbf{c}})-R_{\theta}(\mathcal{G}^{-}|{\mathbf{c}}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>θ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log p(\mathcal{G}^{+}\succ\mathcal{G}^{-}|{\mathbf{c}})=\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(R_{\theta}(\mathcal{G}^{+}|{\mathbf{c}})-R_{\theta}(\mathcal{G}^{-}|{\mathbf{c}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> represent positive and negative groups respectively, with <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{+}\cup\mathcal{G}^{-}=\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{+}\cup\mathcal{G}^{-}=\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{1},\cdots,{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{1},\cdots,{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math> being the complete group of samples for conditioning <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{c}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Intuitively, the objective in <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 Direct Group Preference Optimization ‣ 3 Method ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> can leverage fine-grained preference information of each sample within groups with appropriate parameterization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, we propose parameterizing the group-level reward as a weighted sum of rewards <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\theta}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\theta}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> for each sample within the group:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\theta}(\mathcal{G}|{\mathbf{c}})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot r_{\theta}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\theta}(\mathcal{G}|{\mathbf{c}})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot r_{\theta}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> controls the “importance level” of the sample within the group. The parameterization of group-level reward can reflect the fine-grained information of each sample. And the reward of single sample can be parameterized by following <a href="#S2.E6" title="In DPO Objective ( , ) ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Diffusion-DPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wallace et al., 2024</a>)</cite>:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{\theta}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{\theta}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\beta\log Z({\mathbf{c}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\mathbb{E}_{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\beta\log Z({\mathbf{c}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\beta\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\beta\log Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\beta\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\beta\log Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a intractable partition function. We note that since sampling from the inversion chain <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is expensive, the forward diffusion <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> has been utilized as an approximation in practice <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wallace et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By combining <a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.1 Direct Group Preference Optimization ‣ 3 Method ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 Direct Group Preference Optimization ‣ 3 Method ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we can derive the desired training objective:</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\beta w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})[\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+Z({\mathbf{c}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\beta w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})[\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+Z({\mathbf{c}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\beta w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot[\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+Z({\mathbf{c}})]])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>β</mi><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\beta w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot[\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+Z({\mathbf{c}})]])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E11Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(\beta[\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(\beta[\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E11Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E11Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}})-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}})])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}+\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}})-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}})])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A remaining crucial challenge is that the partition function <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math> is intractable for training. We have to carefully select an appropriate weighting <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each sample to eliminate the intractable partition function <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Generally speaking, a good weighting strategy should satisfy the following:</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Larger weights correspond to better samples in <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and worse samples in <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The weights satisfy: <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}})-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}}))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}})-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})Z({\mathbf{c}}))=0</annotation></semantics></math> for eliminating the intractable <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z({\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z({\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Direct Group Preference Optimization (DGPO)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Diffusion model <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reference model <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Reward model <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, Group size <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, Hyperparameter <math id="alg1.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, Minimum training timestep <math id="alg1.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Learning rate <math id="alg1.l0.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, Iterations <math id="alg1.l0.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, EMA decay <math id="alg1.l0.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> (optional).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Optimized model <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;"># Sample conditioning and generate group</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              Sample conditioning <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{c}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{c}}\sim\mathcal{D}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              Generate group <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{1},...,{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{G}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{1},...,{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{G}\}</annotation></semantics></math> by sampling from <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta^{-}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{c}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta^{-}}(\cdot|{\mathbf{c}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;"># Compute advantages</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{i}\}\leftarrow\{r_{\phi}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{i}\}\leftarrow\{r_{\phi}({\mathbf{c}},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})\}_{i=1}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}\leftarrow\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{r_{j}\})}{\text{std}(\{r_{j}\})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}\leftarrow\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{r_{j}\})}{\text{std}(\{r_{j}\})}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;"># Partition into positive and negative groups</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{+}\leftarrow\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A_{i}&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{+}\leftarrow\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A_{i}&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{-}\leftarrow\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A_{i}\leq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{-}\leftarrow\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A_{i}\leq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#BF0040;"># Compute DGPO loss</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              Sample <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}[t_{\text{min}},T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}[t_{\text{min}},T]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{i}\leftarrow\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}+\sigma_{t}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t}^{i}\leftarrow\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}+\sigma_{t}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
              Compute <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DGPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DGPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DGPO}}</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#S3.E17" title="In 3.2 Advantage-based Weight Design ‣ 3 Method ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
              Update <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta-\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{DGPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DGPO</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta-\eta\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{DGPO}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
              Update <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{-}\leftarrow\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{-}\leftarrow\theta</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{-}\leftarrow\mu\theta^{-}+(1-\mu)\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{-}\leftarrow\mu\theta^{-}+(1-\mu)\theta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Advantage-based Weight Design</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose using advantage-based weights derived from GRPO-style normalization to address the aforementioned issues. Given a group <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}={{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{1},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{2},...,{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>G</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}={{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{1},{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{2},...,{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> with corresponding rewards <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{r_{1},r_{2},...,r_{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{r_{1},r_{2},...,r_{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute advantages:</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A({\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})=\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{r_{j}\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\text{std}(\{r_{j}\}_{j=1}^{G})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>mean</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A({\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})=\frac{r_{i}-\text{mean}(\{r_{j}\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\text{std}(\{r_{j}\}_{j=1}^{G})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">We then partition the group based on advantages:</p>
<table id="S3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{+}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A({\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})&gt;0\},\quad\mathcal{G}^{-}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A({\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})\leq 0\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{+}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A({\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})&gt;0\},\quad\mathcal{G}^{-}=\{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i}:A({\mathbf{x}}_{0}^{i})\leq 0\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">And we set weights as:</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})=|A({\mathbf{x}}_{0})|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})=|A({\mathbf{x}}_{0})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">This choice ensures <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})=\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> due to the zero-mean property of the normalized advantages. It also dynamically assigns larger weights to samples that deviate more from the average, which enables the model to more effectively learn relative preference relationships. More importantly, this weighting turns the objective in <a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.1 Direct Group Preference Optimization ‣ 3 Method ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> to:</p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(\beta[\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\log\sigma(\beta[\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}])." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\mathbb{E}_{q({\mathbf{x}}_{1:T}|{\mathbf{x}}_{0})}\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{0:T}|{\mathbf{c}})}]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p">By using Jensen’s inequality and the convexity of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, we can move the expectation outside:</p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{t,\epsilon}\log\sigma(\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot\beta T\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{t,\epsilon}\log\sigma(\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot\beta T\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot\beta T\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})\cdot\beta T\log\frac{p_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}{p_{\text{ref}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}|{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.8" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\mathcal{G}^{+}\cup\mathcal{G}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>∪</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\mathcal{G}^{+}\cup\mathcal{G}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}+\sigma_{t}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t}=\alpha_{t}{\mathbf{x}}+\sigma_{t}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}=\alpha_{t-1}{\mathbf{x}}+\sigma_{t-1}\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbf{x}}_{t-1}=\alpha_{t-1}{\mathbf{x}}+\sigma_{t-1}\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. We note that to reduce the variance, the sampled noise <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is shared among samples within the same complete groups.
By some simplification, we obtain our final training objective of the proposed DGPO:</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{\text{DGPO}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>DGPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{\text{DGPO}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{t,\epsilon}\log\sigma(-\lambda_{t}\beta T(\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})[L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})-L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>dsm</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>dsm</mtext><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq-\mathbb{E}_{(\mathcal{G}^{+},\mathcal{G}^{-},c)\sim\mathcal{D}}\mathbb{E}_{t,\epsilon}\log\sigma(-\lambda_{t}\beta T(\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{+}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})[L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})-L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})[L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})-L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})]))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>dsm</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>L</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>dsm</mtext></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{{\mathbf{x}}_{0}\in\mathcal{G}^{-}}w({\mathbf{x}}_{0})[L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})-L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})])),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.9" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})=||f_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t,c)-{\mathbf{x}}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>dsm</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})=||f_{\theta}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t,c)-{\mathbf{x}}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})=||f_{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t,c)-{\mathbf{x}}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>dsm</mtext><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{dsm}}^{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}},{\mathbf{x}}_{t},{\mathbf{c}})=||f_{\theta_{\text{ref}}}({\mathbf{x}}_{t},t,c)-{\mathbf{x}}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a weighting function and the constant <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> can be factored into <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The advantage of the derived DGPO objective is fourfold:
1) <span id="S3.SS2.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Leverages Relative information</span>: It directly learns preferences between groups of samples, which leverages the fine-grained relative preference information of individual samples within groups.
2) <span id="S3.SS2.p2.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Enhances training efficiency</span>: It does not require training on the entire sampling trajectory, which notably reduces the computational cost per iteration.
3) <span id="S3.SS2.p2.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Enables effective learning</span>: It sidesteps the need for an inefficient stochastic policy, thus avoiding inefficient model-agnostic exploration and allowing the model to learn more effectively and directly from the preference data.
4) <span id="S3.SS2.p2.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Efficient Sampling and Learning</span>: It allows the usage of deterministic ODE sampling for rollouts. This yields higher-quality training samples compared to inefficient SDE sampling, all while using the same inference budget.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Timestep Clip Strategy</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The considered online setting requires generating samples from the online model which might be expensive; thus, we take a few steps (e.g., 10) for generating samples to reduce the inference cost following Flow-GRPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
However, naively performing DGPO’s training on these samples generated by few steps would lead to serious performance degradation due to the poor sample quality.
To mitigate this, we propose the simple yet effective <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Timestep Clip Strategy</span>: during training, we only sample timesteps from the range <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t_{\text{min}},T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t_{\text{min}},T]</annotation></semantics></math> with a chosen minimum timestep <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\min}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\min}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This could effectively prevent the model from overfitting specific artifacts (e.g., blurriness) of the generated samples by few steps (see ablation in <a href="#S4.F4" title="In Training Cost ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we comprehensively evaluate the proposed DGPO. Specifically, we benchmark improvements on three tasks—compositional image generation, visual text rendering, and human preference alignment (<a href="#S4.T1" title="In 4 Experiments ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tables</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). We also present qualitative comparisons and training efficiency (<a href="#S1.F2" title="In 1 Introduction ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Training Cost ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). We further conduct ablations on key components (<a href="#S4.F5" title="In Compared to Diffusion DPO ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Training Cost ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Reinforcing Diffusion Models by Direct Group Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
